  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "final-note",
      "page": "final",
      "x": 1000,
      "y": 1400,
      "w": 520,
      "text": "Final direction. Tool cards expand in place for options, General is a second view inside the same panel with a back chevron. Menubar icon has three states: idle, listening (tiny meter), recording (red timer). Tokens are in design/DESIGN.md."
    },
    {
      "id": "v2-note",
      "page": "v2",
      "x": 1280,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 300,
      "text": "Round 2. Geist only, no serif. Bar meters instead of curves. Recent rows use a tile per item: mic tile for a transcript, thumbnail for a recording. Amber accent throughout; only the ground (background, panel, card, text tint) changes between artboards."
    },
    {
      "id": "concept-note",
      "page": "concept",
      "x": 1240,
      "y": 660,
      "w": 280,
      "text": "Ink and amber, custom chrome. The panel is the whole app: tool cards expand in place for options, so there is no Settings window. Keycaps show the shortcut. The pill grows into a card while transcribing so you see words land before the paste."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-a",
      "page": "directions",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 800,
      "text": "A \u00b7 Ink and amber. Warm near-black, one amber accent, serif for titles only. Feels like a crafted tool, ages well. Tradeoff: amber on dark is low-contrast for small secondary text, and the serif can read as precious if overused."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-b",
      "page": "directions",
      "x": 900,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 800,
      "text": "B \u00b7 Glass. Deep indigo ground, frosted layers, periwinkle accent, large radii. Most 'modern' and most in step with current macOS. Tradeoff: blur and translucency are expensive to get right in AppKit, and it dates fastest."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-c",
      "page": "directions",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1780,
      "w": 800,
      "text": "C \u00b7 Paper. Light, warm off-white, one coral accent, dark pill for contrast. Friendliest and most sellable to non-developers. Tradeoff: light-first means you design dark mode second, and it is the least 'yours' at a glance."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-d",
      "page": "directions",
      "x": 900,
      "y": 1780,
      "w": 800,
      "text": "D \u00b7 Terminal. Green-black, lime accent, mono for labels, tight radii. Unmistakably a developer tool, dense and fast. Tradeoff: narrowest audience, and lime as the only accent leaves no room for status colours."
    },
    {
      "id": "scope-note",
      "page": "v1",
      "x": 1120,
      "y": 190,
      "w": 260,
      "text": "v1 surfaces only. Dark appearance drawn; light follows system automatically in the real app. No onboarding, no library window, no General pane yet."
    }
  ],
  "launch": {
    "view": "canvas",
    "page": "final"
  }
